# Local environment example — placeholders only, never real secrets.
#
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in values:
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env
#
# The Node.js services do NOT load this file automatically — export the
# service variables into each service process environment, or use the
# launchers that do load it: `pnpm dev` for the API Gateway and
# `pnpm usage` for Platform Usage.

# --- API Gateway (local development) ---
# PORT=3000
# HOST=127.0.0.1

# --- Internal service authentication ---
# One strong random value shared by local processes, e.g.
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# The AI Platform launcher accepts the same shared value, so Gateway and
# Orchestrator agree without a second authority for service identities.
# INTERNAL_SERVICE_TOKEN=change-me-local-only
# Pair-specific override (optional; wins when set):
# AI_ORCHESTRATOR_INTERNAL_TOKEN=

# --- AI Orchestrator URL ---
# The launcher enforces http://127.0.0.1:3003 when unset. Never rely on the
# service default (port 3001 addresses the Model Registry, not the
# Orchestrator). An operator-set value must parse as http(s) and must not
# use port 3001.
# ORCHESTRATOR_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3003

# --- Gateway JWT verification (must match the local issuer) ---
# JWKS_URI=http://127.0.0.1:4567/.well-known/jwks.json
# JWT_ISSUER=http://127.0.0.1:4567
# JWT_AUDIENCE defaults to oicunt-platform when unset:
# JWT_AUDIENCE=

# --- Platform Usage service (opt-in; see docs/development.md) ---
# Recommended start: `pnpm usage`. That launcher loads this file, validates
# the settings below, enforces a loopback-only bind at
# http://127.0.0.1:8090 (refusing conflicting USAGE_SERVICE_HOST/PORT),
# refuses NODE_ENV=production, and never applies migrations. The raw
# entrypoint (services/usage/dist/start.js) also works but binds all
# interfaces (0.0.0.0) unless USAGE_SERVICE_HOST is set explicitly.
# The standalone entrypoint fails closed: it refuses to boot unless ALL of
# the following are set and valid, and it never falls back to in-memory
# repositories or queues:
#   - an internal token (precedence: PLATFORM_USAGE_INTERNAL_TOKEN, then
#     INTERNAL_SERVICE_TOKEN, then USAGE_INTERNAL_TOKEN). The value is the
#     HS256 HMAC signing secret for signed internal service JWTs
#     (aud platform-usage, sub api-gateway); it is never sent as a raw
#     request token.
#   - PostgreSQL access (USAGE_DB_* always wins over DATABASE_*)
#   - a RabbitMQ broker URL (amqp:// or amqps://; there is NO implicit
#     guest@localhost default)
# USE_DATABASE=false and USE_RABBITMQ=false are refused at startup.
# Bind host for the raw entrypoint (the launcher forces 127.0.0.1):
# USAGE_SERVICE_HOST=127.0.0.1
# HTTP port for the raw entrypoint (the launcher forces 8090),
# integer 1-65535 (default 8090):
# USAGE_SERVICE_PORT=8090
# Usage database (USAGE_DB_* overrides DATABASE_* when both are set):
# USAGE_DB_HOST=
# USAGE_DB_PORT=
# USAGE_DB_NAME=oicunt_usage
# USAGE_DB_USER=
# USAGE_DB_PASSWORD=
# Broker (required; the consumer attaches during startup):
# RABBITMQ_URL=
# PLATFORM_USAGE_INTERNAL_TOKEN=
# Migrations: routine startup NEVER applies migrations — it only performs
# a read-only schema compatibility verification (ledger + critical
# tables/columns) and refuses to serve traffic if the deployed schema does
# not match the build. Schema changes require the deliberate command below,
# run after a database backup:
#   pnpm --filter @oicunt/service-usage migrate
# or equivalently: node services/usage/dist/migrate.js

# --- Usage admission (leave unset for the ordinary dev workflow) ---
# Setting ENABLE_USAGE_ADMISSION=true requires the Platform Usage service,
# which `pnpm dev` never starts: run it separately with `pnpm usage`. The
# dev launcher refuses to start while the flag is set.
# Activation is explicit: development defaults to disabled; production
# requires ENABLE_USAGE_ADMISSION to be explicitly 'true' or 'false' and
# fails startup otherwise (never implied by NODE_ENV). Any other value
# fails startup in every environment.
# USAGE_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090
